# Single-page app. Anything that is not a real file and not an API route gets
# the empty shell (dist/app.html), and the router takes it from there.
#
# Deliberately not /index.html: that document has the landing page prerendered
# into it, so handing it to /login means the browser parses thirty kilobytes of
# a page it is about to throw away. Real assets, including "/", are matched
# before this rule, so the prerendered landing still wins at the root.
#
# The target is extensionless on purpose. Pages 308s /app.html to /app, and a
# rewrite whose target redirects is a rewrite that does not happen.
/*  /app  200
